Package: selectiveHotelling
Title: Selective Hotelling T-squared Testing After Clustering with
    Unknown Covariance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yiqun", "Chen", , "yiqun.t.chen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Valid selective inference for a Hotelling T-squared test comparing
    the means of two clusters discovered by a data-driven clustering algorithm,
    treating the covariance matrix as unknown. For k-means clustering, Monte
    Carlo p-values are computed by sampling the polar factor uniformly within
    the data-driven selection region on the Stiefel manifold, extending the
    selective inference framework of Chen and Witten (2023) to the
    unknown-covariance setting. An algorithm-agnostic exact test based on the
    Besag and Clifford (1991) serial Monte Carlo construction supports
    arbitrary clustering routines, including hierarchical clustering, by
    sampling along a reversible Markov chain on the Stiefel manifold restricted
    to the selection event.
